      "message": "Understood. I find the pointer confusing as it is generally used for objects that are mutable and/or objects that are large and expensive to copy and/or objects that require a unique identity. None of those apply in this case.\n\nCan you not replicate that 3 state in OptionalPath?\n\nPath is valid - path!\u003dnil, reason\u003d\"\"\nPath is not valid but not an error - path\u003dnil, reason\u003d\"\"\nPath is in error - path\u003dnil, reason!\u003d\"\"\n\nOr maybe create a new type (cannot think of a good name at the moment) which embeds an OptionalPath and adds the reason?",
